// Second `SpriteSummon` player spell -- see glyph_of_warding.ron's own
// comment for the full pilot writeup of what this variant can and can't do
// (no energy_cost field, no damage/buff/trigger capability at all, only
// `CreateSpriteEvent` placement). Same real gap applies here, plus one more:
// D&D's "a second glyph elsewhere, linked so triggering one fires the
// other's stored effect" has no cross-reference mechanism between two
// separate ability casts whatsoever -- there is no way for one `SpriteSummon`
// invocation to know about, or affect, sprites placed by an earlier one.
// That entire "linked" half of the spell's concept is dropped, not
// approximated.
//
// The sheet gives no aoe/range for this spell (unlike glyph_of_warding's
// explicit `Sphere r6`), consistent with "a single trigger-glyph" rather
// than a warded area -- so this ships as a single, dense marker at the
// touched spot (`summon_distance: (0, 1)`, `sparseness: 0.0`) instead of
// glyph_of_warding's wider ring, using the same `EnsnaringVines` obstruction
// sprite for the same "physically awkward to walk through" secondary
// footprint, and the same long `del_timeout` lingering window.
SpriteSummon(
    buildup_duration: 0.6,
    cast_duration: 0.4,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    sprite: EnsnaringVines,
    del_timeout: Some((600.0, 60.0)),
    summon_distance: (0.0, 1.0),
    sparseness: 0.0,
    angle: 360.0,
    anchor: Summoner,
    move_efficiency: 1.0,
    ori_modifier: 1.0,
    meta: (school: Some(Abjuration), source: Some(Arcane)),
)
